{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5cz6af2Nj2svx2MAHam","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary of Repository Findings:\n\n**Shipment entity** (`Shipment.kt:9-14`): Data class with shipmentId, orderId, carrier, and status fields.\n\n**ShipmentStatus enum** (`Shipment.kt:23-27`): Three values—CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED.\n\n**Repository** (`ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27`): In-memory store with save(), findById(), existsById() methods.\n\n**Controller** (`ShipmentController.kt:20-56`): POST create, GET by id, GET list. Uses exception-throwing pattern.\n\n**Error handling** (`ApiExceptions.kt:19-24`): ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404).\n\n**ErrorCode enum** (`ApiError.kt:31-37`): Currently has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED. Missing: error code for invalid shipment state.\n\n**Testing** (`ShipmentControllerTest.kt:1-85`): Uses MockMvc with status checks and jsonPath assertions.\n\n## Conventions This Repository Has:\n\n- Errors are signaled by throwing ApiException subclasses (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException)\n- ErrorCode enum defines the machine-readable error codes\n- GlobalExceptionHandler converts exceptions to ApiError envelopes\n- Controllers return ResponseEntity for success, throw exceptions for failure\n- Tests use MockMvc with fluent assertion chains and jsonPath matchers\n\n## Affected Files (Cannot Be Avoided):\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Need to add SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code for the CANCELLED rejection case\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Need to add the POST confirm endpoint\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Need to add tests for confirm endpoint\n\n## Risks:\n\n- Breaking existing tests by not preserving backward compatibility\n- Incorrect HTTP status code selection for the CANCELLED case\n- Not implementing idempotency correctly (CONFIRMED shipment must not fail on retry)\n- Forgetting to persist the state change to the repository\n\n## Open Questions:\n\nNone—all requirements are unambiguous.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` error code to the ErrorCode enum. This will be thrown when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID; throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return unchanged (idempotent success)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS code\n   - Return the updated (or unchanged) Shipment with HTTP 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test cases:\n   - `confirms_a_created_shipment_to_confirmed_status` — POST confirm on CREATED → HTTP 200 with CONFIRMED status\n   - `confirms_an_already_confirmed_shipment_idempotently` — POST confirm on CONFIRMED → HTTP 200 with CONFIRMED status (verify no error)\n   - `rejects_confirming_a_cancelled_shipment` — POST confirm on CANCELLED → HTTP 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code\n   - `rejects_confirming_a_nonexistent_shipment` — POST confirm on missing ID → HTTP 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\n- **Service layer** — Adding a ShipmentService class to encapsulate confirm logic. Rejected because the existing codebase has no service layer; logic is directly in controllers. The ticket says \"preserve the existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture,\" which means keeping the current simple structure.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED):**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n   - Controller retrieves shipment via repository.findById()\n   - Status is CREATED; create new Shipment with status=CONFIRMED\n   - repository.save() persists the change\n   - Response: HTTP 200 + updated Shipment JSON\n\n2. **Idempotent case (already CONFIRMED):**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n   - Controller retrieves shipment via repository.findById()\n   - Status is CONFIRMED; return shipment unchanged\n   - Response: HTTP 200 + unchanged Shipment JSON (no error)\n\n3. **Conflict case (CANCELLED):**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n   - Controller retrieves shipment via repository.findById()\n   - Status is CANCELLED; throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS, ...)\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches, converts to ApiError with status 409\n   - Response: HTTP 409 + ApiError envelope\n\n4. **Not found case:**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/missing/confirm\n   - Controller calls repository.findById() → returns null\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...)\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches, converts to ApiError with status 404\n   - Response: HTTP 404 + ApiError envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **Test 1 (happy path):** Create S-1 in CREATED status, confirm it, assert status becomes CONFIRMED and response is HTTP 200\n- **Test 2 (idempotency):** Create S-2 in CREATED status, confirm it, confirm again, assert both return CONFIRMED with HTTP 200 (second call must not error)\n- **Test 3 (cancelled conflict):** Create S-3, manually inject CANCELLED status via repository, confirm, assert HTTP 409 and error code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n- **Test 4 (not found):** POST confirm on non-existent ID, assert HTTP 404 and error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me now implement the changes:\n\n**Step 1: Add the error code**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1829,"cache_read_input_tokens":16612,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1829},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac8537a8-32a5-470f-8af8-75b8ddf05c94","uuid":"c55e245f-637b-4385-b7d9-7a26ca1c53c6","timestamp":"2026-09-15T17:30:02.669Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5cz69ro7coFjXsWgyjR"}
